.TH "GLESHA-CHECK" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-check \- test access to remote buckets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha check\fR \-\-to REMOTE... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each remote, write a small object under glesha/check/, read its metadata and content back, and delete it. Each step is reported as OK, FAILED, or SKIPPED. An object that could not be deleted is named in the report.
.PP
A bucket with a default Object Lock retention is not written to, and its check fails.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Test REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory, or 128MiB). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. On Linux, the default is half of the available memory. On other systems, or if the available memory cannot be read, the default is 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha check \-\-to aws,b2
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-upload (1)
